s=s.replace("""# Put the person on hold, or take them off it when held. The audit line is written once it is saved,
# then the rollup lines: holding takes the person's OPEN claims out of every live total, releasing
# puts them back. No such person (404) writes nothing.
load:""","""# Add a hold to the person from a date (blank: the sheet's today) to an optional to-date. The audit line
# is written once it is saved, then the rollup lines: the hold takes the person's OPEN and PENDING claims
# dated within it, unless bound by a statement, out of every live total. There is no release: a hold ends
# on its to-date. A bad date or a to-date before the from-date (400), or no such person (404), writes nothing.
validate:
  class: net.officefloor.hq.app.person.ValidateHold
  next: load
load:""")
open(f,'w').write(s)
EOF
